			"Message": "docs(Land): Document per-subsystem routing tiers and normalize shell formatting across Maintain scripts\n\nRewrite TierGatedImplementationSelection.md with the complete per-subsystem routing tier table spanning TierTerminal through TierWebSocket, documenting the two-layer tier architecture (infrastructure Cargo features + per-subsystem runtime dispatch), flavor overlay workflow via `--flavor RustOnly|NodeFirst|Full`, TierEnvironment.sh propagation path, mod.rs compile-time dispatch using `tier_routes_to_node`, and expanded failure modes including flavor override surprises.\n\nNormalize redirect operators (`2>/dev/null` → `2> /dev/null`) and case-statement indentation across all 24 Maintain shell scripts, bringing them into consistent alignment with the shell-formatting convention established in the prior flavor-overlay commit.\n\nAdd `proc-macro2` with `span-locations` to Cargo.toml for improved proc-macro backtrace resolution. Restore `packageManager: pnpm@11.3.0` in package.json alongside `@tauri-apps/cli` dev dependency, and set `nodeLinker: hoisted` in pnpm-workspace.yaml for correct pnpm dependency resolution. Register `MountainWebSocketPort` and `MountainWebSocketSecret` in turbo.json globalEnv so Turborepo invalidates build caches when these runtime variables change.",
			"SHA": "ff07b97e6f4ad62bf1fc3b58c43d7105aa5ca49f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T13:51:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				29
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Add tier flavor overlay system and normalize shell formatting\n\nIntroduce three tier-routing flavor overlays (RustOnly, NodeFirst, Full) that source per-subsystem Tier* values via `--flavor`/`-f` on Debug/Build.sh and Release/Build.sh, propagating into Mountain's build.rs and Cocoon's esbuild defines. The Flavors toggle between Mountain-native, Cocoon-Node, or hybrid Mist WebSocket IPC at compile time without profile duplication.\n\n- `.env.Land.RustOnly`: Every subsystem with a native Mountain implementation routes through Rust (Tier*=Mountain).\n- `.env.Land.NodeFirst`: All API surfaces route to Cocoon Node.js, leaving Mountain as a thin IPC pass-through for upstream VS Code feature debugging.\n- `.env.Land.Full`: Full-production routing with NodeDeferred fallback and Mist WebSocket transport enabled.\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to bring DAP inline debugging, webview panel persistence across nativeHost:reload, compile-time tier routing dispatch, Mist WebSocket transport on port 5051, 30-second git subprocess timeout, and crash-safe memento hydration.\n\nNormalize shell formatting across all Maintain scripts: convert case-statement indentation to consistent style, fix redirect spacing (2>/dev/null), and align pipeline continuations. Add new Tier* env vars and flavor overlay files to turbo.json cache inputs and env passthrough for Turborepo correctness.\n\nBuild and run tooling now accepts a `--flavor` flag for quick tier configuration switching without editing profile declarations.",
			"SHA": "b79ff8acab516d29ae2c51a9f03936adeec376f3"
		},
